                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "80d193fb-5128-4d17-9227-b0bfcf17cbae",
                        "entry_id": "e5b5b94d-e1e1-3d9c-ab59-86d54050467c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "moonlings"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b4252c22-37a3-3c22-a948-a0eff334068c",
                        "entry_id": "e5b5b94d-e1e1-3d9c-ab59-86d54050467c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A simpleton; a lunatic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "338bd407-3fff-421e-ba5a-3f6fce9445dd",
                                "sense_id": "b4252c22-37a3-3c22-a948-a0eff334068c",
                                "text": "I have a husband, and a two-legg'd one, But such a moonling, as no wit of man, Or roses can redeem from being an ass."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2eed870-ecf4-4fd3-a8fe-b003f0ce78bb",
                                "sense_id": "b4252c22-37a3-3c22-a948-a0eff334068c",
                                "text": "Of the members composing this household, there are but two of whom it will be necessary to speak in this connection; and these are the moonling, or simpleton, and the sister of the wife."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b489e6af-0a83-43cd-aec8-af7971bd59d2",
                                "sense_id": "b4252c22-37a3-3c22-a948-a0eff334068c",
                                "text": "But allow me to say that you were standing like a moonling on that road."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b6ebdca-c1d4-454f-9e64-a4c266644f0f",
                                "sense_id": "b4252c22-37a3-3c22-a948-a0eff334068c",
                                "text": "\"Jack is n-not a moonling,\" Catherine said. \"His m-mother became ill before his birth. He c-cannot be blamed for any mental deficiency.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7f7cdca9-4432-3c1e-b324-44fa2b6113f0",
                        "entry_id": "e5b5b94d-e1e1-3d9c-ab59-86d54050467c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who is lovesick; one who moons over a beloved."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "256ad13a-22e5-4daf-b625-8e991f537418",
                                "sense_id": "7f7cdca9-4432-3c1e-b324-44fa2b6113f0",
                                "text": "The sky was not quite as blue as her—Thunderation, he was no moonling!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58354ce3-e8d0-4b37-9add-251086f27c60",
                                "sense_id": "7f7cdca9-4432-3c1e-b324-44fa2b6113f0",
                                "text": "Remaining there long enough to hear Those words that moonling longs to hear...I love you"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b61a88bd-af28-4966-90a0-11bd44b97020",
                                "sense_id": "7f7cdca9-4432-3c1e-b324-44fa2b6113f0",
                                "text": "Here he was, reputed to be a rake among rakes, but he discovered, where Thea was concerned, he was as vulnerable and uncertain as the greenest moonling in love for the first time."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "36fe38cb-290f-39b9-8608-75f956299a31",
                        "entry_id": "e5b5b94d-e1e1-3d9c-ab59-86d54050467c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A changeling."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bac2aec-c23c-4e1b-9cf2-17939a63cf4d",
                                "sense_id": "36fe38cb-290f-39b9-8608-75f956299a31",
                                "text": "\"I see. He's a black man. But Jacob Millhaven is not black. Eldridge was left on his doorstep as a baby, and the philosopher adopted him.\" \"Oh! Then he's a moonling! He doesn't seem to suffer from any stigma.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a0d4907f-aa3c-3fdb-bce2-aa0403bbabbe",
                        "entry_id": "e5b5b94d-e1e1-3d9c-ab59-86d54050467c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone from the Moon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bee456c8-7954-4d6e-9d7e-c5dcc9b6e770",
                                "sense_id": "a0d4907f-aa3c-3fdb-bce2-aa0403bbabbe",
                                "text": "A shy moonling hangs on the suit of an astronaut and is taken back to earth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ea363e3-6595-4b12-84da-3eb676461bba",
                                "sense_id": "a0d4907f-aa3c-3fdb-bce2-aa0403bbabbe",
                                "text": "For a given walking speed, will an earthling astronaut or a moonling do less, equal, or more work when taking a stroll on the Moon, and by what factor?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ed480f6-605a-4a2a-b39a-7102d47065e9",
                                "sense_id": "a0d4907f-aa3c-3fdb-bce2-aa0403bbabbe",
                                "text": "This, together with the 'balloon manufactured entirely of dirty newspaper' in which the dwarf/moonling descends at the tale's opening, points to some self-referential satire on behalf of Poe, a newspaperman himself."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
